    "id": "788f6fabb1da67c6",
    "type": "comment",
    "z": "aff20ddf043031dc",
    "name": "Centrifuge: map subscription",
    "info": "Prerequisites: a Centrifugo v6 server on ws://localhost:8000. The repository ships one: edit quickstart/centrifugo.yaml (set client.token.hmac_secret_key), then run `centrifugo --config quickstart/centrifugo.yaml`. Its `kv` namespace (subscription_type map, mode persistent) already allows client subscribe, map_publish and map_remove, so this example works unmodified.\n\nOpen the `centrifuge server` configuration, paste the server's `client.token.hmac_secret_key` into Secret, and deploy.\n\nExpected: the `centrifuge in` node shows `subscribed` and its debug output first shows a `sync` snapshot (empty on a fresh server). Click \"set sensor-1\": a `centrifuge out` node in map_publish mode sets key `sensor-1` to `{\"temperature\":21.5}` on channel `kv:board`, the `centrifuge in` node's debug shows an `update` event with that key and data, and \"set acknowledged\" shows `msg.centrifuge = {\"action\":\"map_publish\",\"channel\":\"kv:board\",\"key\":\"sensor-1\"}`. Click \"remove sensor-1\": the same key is removed, the `centrifuge in` node's debug shows an `update` event with `removed: true` and `payload: null`, and \"remove acknowledged\" shows `msg.centrifuge = {\"action\":\"map_remove\",\"channel\":\"kv:board\",\"key\":\"sensor-1\"}`.",
    "x": 200,
    "y": 40,
    "wires": []
  },
